;; Reviewed 2026-10-11 by the user (written by Claude, from design
;; section 7 and the guest runs). Why this is right:
;; - The fourth line shows how First16's read-only parameter, an ARRAY
;;   16 OF CHAR, was passed: the procedure changes the caller's c16 and
;;   then reads its parameter. LLVM passes one of at most 16 bytes by
;;   value, so it still reads "s"; the VAX backend passes every read-only
;;   record or array by reference, uncopied (design section 7, decided
;;   2026-10-06), so it reads the "*". language-extensions.md, "Read-only
;;   parameters", says a program may not rely on which; the fixture pins
;;   LLVM's rule only.
;; - Every other line is LLVM's. The same under -O2 and -OC.
7 11  2
5  3  9 14  5  0
42 42
**
104 107  -9
111  8
